      "name": "test_greedy_lower_bound",
      "intent": "Implement a left-to-right greedy that always cuts left if possible (x_i - h_i > last_occupied), else right if possible (x_i + h_i < next tree's x or no next tree), else leaves the tree. Count how many trees it cuts. Assert that the program's output is at least that count."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_upper_bound",
      "intent": "Compute the number of trees that satisfy either 'can fall left' (x_i - h_i > x_{i-1} or i==1) or 'can fall right' (x_i + h_i < x_{i+1} or i==n). Assert the program's output is at most this number."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_lower_bound",
      "intent": "Compute L1 = number of trees that can fall left without hitting previous tree (x_i - h_i > x_{i-1} or i==1). Compute L2 = number that can fall right without hitting next tree (x_i + h_i < x_{i+1} or i==n). Let L = max(L1, L2). Assert the program's output is at least L."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_shift_small",
