{
  "rationale": "The tests combine simple sanity checks (bounds, integer validity), structural invariants (diameter unchanged under vertex relabeling), special-case certificates (path, star), and a full recomputation of the diameter using a standard algorithm. The metamorphic relations rely on the specification's implicit assumption that the graph's topology, not its labeling, determines the answer. The lower- and upper-bound tests follow from the triangle inequality in trees. The full recomputation is the strongest catch-all; if forced to drop one, the second permutation test would be the first to go, as it repeats the idea of label invariance with a different permutation.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "name": "test_valid_integer",
